{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SVmgg63Ev1dJa3bUf1yxHa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Phase 2 (Hardening + llm.py upgrades) â€” Description\n2\t\n3\t**North Star:** Close the two security/judgment tripwires on Aurora's LIVE verdict path AND adopt\n4\tthe cheap modern Anthropic API capabilities Aurora is missing â€” *evolving `llm.py` and the security\n5\tpath, NOT rebuilding the architecture*. This is the build half of the researchPrime AuroraTwo verdict\n6\t(`docs/AURORA_AURORATWO_RESEARCH.md`): fan-out is theater at TOP_K=2-3; the value is in the LLM layer\n7\t+ the security/evidence path, both of which already exist and only need hardening/upgrading.\n8\t\n9\tTwo threads, one sequential run (they overlap on `orchestrator.py` + the security judge, so they run\n10\tin series, not parallel):\n11\t- **Security hardening (H1-H2):** payload-depth re-scan superseding the served-text backfill\n12\t  (monotonic toward non-servable); promote the evidence-rigor loop out of shadow with a real metered\n13\t  per-iteration score_fn + an engine-diff CLI + a tightened promotion gate (defaults to legacy).\n14\t- **llm.py upgrades (L1-L6):** a cost-telemetry substrate first (so discount features are metered\n15\t  correctly), then prompt caching, structured outputs, adaptive-`effort` thinking, model retargeting,\n16\t  and the Message Batches API.\n17\t\n18\t## Success criteria\n19\t- Every servable artifact carries a payload-depth `security_status`; benign-description/malicious-payload is caught; the re-stamp is monotonic toward non-servable.\n20\t- The evidence loop has a real metered per-iteration score_fn + a runnable `bin/engine-diff.py` enforcing the promotion gate; the live flip stays default-off.\n21\t- `llm.py` supports prompt caching, structured outputs, adaptive `effort`, current model tiers, and an opt-in batch path â€” all with correct CostRecorderâ†’pricing.yaml metering (regression-tested).\n22\t- Locked-preserved intact: KB schema + library, single-owner security gate, deterministic cost telemetry, Helping Hand + publisher.\n23\t\n24\t## Hard constraints\n25\t- Both security waves touch the LIVE verdict path: no seam may produce an unearned pass; the gate stays single-owner (`roles/security/gate.py`).\n26\t- The metered evidence-shadow batch (SA-1) and the live promotion flip (SA-2) are SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED and OUT of the build waves â€” waves build machinery + run shadow only.\n27\t- Every LLM call meters through CostRecorder against a matching pricing.yaml key; the Sonnetâ†’Haiku fallback, tenacity retry, and `AURORA_DISABLE_GEMINI` kill-switch are preserved.\n28\t- test-command: `python -m pytest`. No test weakening; the test count may only rise.\n29\t\n30\t## Provenance\n31\tSource plans (committed): `docs/AURORA_HARDENING_PLAN.md` (H1-H2) and `docs/AURORA_LLM_UPGRADES_PLAN.md`\n32\t(L1-L6), each code-grounded by a Plan sub-agent. Combined + ordered here for Foreman.\n33\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3ebcf08-c961-4db6-8228-86ade240a49d","uuid":"2812fc91-6766-47f1-9d7b-3edaced2ca1c","timestamp":"2026-06-13T12:51:42.204Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\aurora\\docs\\foreman-handoff-phase2\\DESCRIPTION.md","content":"# Aurora Phase 2 (Hardening + llm.py upgrades) â€” Description\n\n**North Star:** Close the two security/judgment tripwires on Aurora's LIVE verdict path AND adopt\nthe cheap modern Anthropic API capabilities Aurora is missing â€” *evolving `llm.py` and the security\npath, NOT rebuilding the architecture*. This is the build half of the researchPrime AuroraTwo verdict\n(`docs/AURORA_AURORATWO_RESEARCH.md`): fan-out is theater at TOP_K=2-3; the value is in the LLM layer\n+ the security/evidence path, both of which already exist and only need hardening/upgrading.\n\nTwo threads, one sequential run (they overlap on `orchestrator.py` + the security judge, so they run\nin series, not parallel):\n- **Security hardening (H1-H2):** payload-depth re-scan superseding the served-text backfill\n  (monotonic toward non-servable); promote the evidence-rigor loop out of shadow with a real metered\n  per-iteration score_fn + an engine-diff CLI + a tightened promotion gate (defaults to legacy).\n- **llm.py upgrades (L1-L6):** a cost-telemetry substrate first (so discount features are metered\n  correctly), then prompt caching, structured outputs, adaptive-`effort` thinking, model retargeting,\n  and the Message Batches API.\n\n## Success criteria\n- Every servable artifact carries a payload-depth `security_status`; benign-description/malicious-payload is caught; the re-stamp is monotonic toward non-servable.\n- The evidence loop has a real metered per-iteration score_fn + a runnable `bin/engine-diff.py` enforcing the promotion gate; the live flip stays default-off.\n- `llm.py` supports prompt caching, structured outputs, adaptive `effort`, current model tiers, and an opt-in batch path â€” all with correct CostRecorderâ†’pricing.yaml metering (regression-tested).\n- Locked-preserved intact: KB schema + library, single-owner security gate, deterministic cost telemetry, Helping Hand + publisher.\n\n## Hard constraints\n- Both security waves touch the LIVE verdict path: no seam may produce an unearned pass; the gate stays single-owner (`roles/security/gate.py`).\n- The metered evidence-shadow batch (SA-1) and the live promotion flip (SA-2) are SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED and OUT of the build waves â€” waves build machinery + run shadow only.\n- Every LLM call meters through CostRecorder against a matching pricing.yaml key; the Sonnetâ†’Haiku fallback, tenacity retry, and `AURORA_DISABLE_GEMINI` kill-switch are preserved.\n- test-command: `python -m pytest`. No test weakening; the test count may only rise.\n\n## Provenance\nSource plans (committed): `docs/AURORA_HARDENING_PLAN.md` (H1-H2) and `docs/AURORA_LLM_UPGRADES_PLAN.md`\n(L1-L6), each code-grounded by a Plan sub-agent. Combined + ordered here for Foreman.\n","numLines":33,"startLine":1,"totalLines":33}}}
