red_outputs.py`.\n147\t\n148\t**Depends on:** Wave 4\n149\t\n150\t**done-when:** Those paths request schema-guaranteed JSON, parse without fence-stripping, an off-schema\n151\tjudge response still fails closed to `abstain`, metering unchanged.\n152\t\n153\t- **Given** a schema-valid response, **then** no `strip_fences` path is taken.\n154\t- **Given** an off-schema/empty judge response, **then** the family is `abstain` and the panel stays fail-closed.\n155\t- **Given** any structured-output call, **then** the cost row matches Wave 3/4 (no `test_pricing_keys` regression).\n156\t\n157\t## Wave 6 â€” L4: Adaptive thinking via `effort` (drop deprecated budget_tokens)\n158\t\n159\t**Intent:** Adopt adaptive thinking through `effort`; never send `budget_tokens` (deprecated on 4.6+;\n160\tOpus 4.8 returns 400); meter thinking tokens correctly.\n161\t\n162\t**Deliverables:** `llm.py` `call_anthropic` `effort: Optional[str]` mapping to the adaptive-thinking\n163\trequest shape; a guard that fails loudly if a `budget_tokens` field is ever assembled for an Anthropic\n164\trequest; fold API-reported thinking tokens into metered output (mirror the Gemini `thoughts_token_count`\n165\tfold â€” root cause of the prior $118 incident); Gemini `thinking_budget=0` guard untouched; optional\n166\tconservative `effort` on critic_a/reconciler/judge (default unset = current behavior); new\n167\t`tests/test_effort_thinking.py`.\n168\t\n169\t**Depends on:** Wave 5\n170\t\n171\t**done-when:** Anthropic path supports `effort`, provably never sends `budget_tokens`, folds thinking\n172\ttokens into metered output, Gemini guard untouched, suite green.\n173\t\n174\t- **Given** any `call_anthropic`, **then** the request contains no `budget_tokens` field. [SUBTLE â€” the 400-on-Opus-4.8 trap]\n175\t- **Given** a response reporting thinking tokens, **then** they are folded into metered output (not dropped).\n176\t- **Given** `effort` unset, **then** behavior + cost identical to pre-wave.\n177\t\n178\t## Wave 7 â€” L5: Model retargeting to current tiers + 4.7+ tokenizer cost factor\n179\t\n180\t**Intent:** Retarget default model tags to current tiers (Opus 4.x / Sonnet 4.6 / Haiku 4.5) and add\n181\tthe ~35%-more-tokens 4.7+ tokenizer factor so cost telemetry stays accurate.\n182\t\n183\t**Deliverables:** `kb/pricing.yaml` add the current Opus tier with cache sub-rates + `verification:`,\n184\treconcile `default_models`/role defaults, add `tokenizer_factor` (default 1.0; 1.35 for 4.7+); `llm.py`\n185\tapply `tokenizer_factor` ONLY to pre-call estimates, NEVER to post-call metering (real `resp.usage`\n186\tstays ground-truth), document the distinction; `orchestrator.py` per-role defaults + role model\n187\tconstants point to retargeted tags via existing `AURORA_*_MODEL` env overrides (no hardcode drift),\n188\t`HAIKU_DEFAULT` stays a real priced tag; extend `tests/test_pricing_keys.py`.\n189\t\n190\t**Depends on:** Wave 6\n191\t\n192\t**done-when:** All default tags resolve to priced keys, the tokenizer factor adjusts estimates only,\n193\t`test_pricing_keys.py` passes with new tags.\n194\t\n195\t- **Given** every retargeted tag, **then** `lookup_rates` hits a non-$0 priced key.\n196\t- **Given** a 4.7+ model, **then** the factor applies to estimates but NOT to recorded actuals. [SUBTLE]\n197\t- **Given** the retargeting, **then** fallback / kill-switch / gate tests stay green.\n198\t\n199\t## Wave 8 â€” L6: Message Batches API for non-interactive nightly sweeps\n200\t\n201\t**Intent:** Opt-in async Message Batches path for the nightly sweeps (~50% discount); synchronous path\n202\tstays the default; correct batch-discounted metering preserved.\n203\t\n204\t**Deliverables:** `llm.py` `submit_anthropic_batch(...)` + poll/collect reusing `_is_retryable_anthropic`,\n205\teach result recording `CostRecorder.record(... batch_mode=True)` from real per-result usage (incl. Wave-4\n206\tcache fields); a single-request batch failure degrades to synchronous `call_anthropic`