try (CostRecorderâ†’pricing.yaml), Helping Hand +\npublisher. Both security waves touch the LIVE verdict path: no seam may produce an unearned pass. The\nmetered evidence-shadow batch (SA-1) and the live promotion flip (SA-2) are SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED and\nOUT of these waves. No test weakening; the count may only rise.\n\n> Waves run in series (the threads overlap on `orchestrator.py` + the security judge). Wave 1-2 =\n> security hardening; Wave 3-8 = llm.py upgrades, cost-telemetry substrate first so discount features\n> are metered correctly. Full per-thread rationale + code-grounded findings live in the source plans\n> `docs/AURORA_HARDENING_PLAN.md` and `docs/AURORA_LLM_UPGRADES_PLAN.md`.\n\n## Wave 1 â€” H1: Payload-depth security scan (supersede the served-text backfill)\n\n**Intent:** Replace the W2 served-text baseline (every artifact stamped `clean-with-notes` from\nname + short_description) with a scan of each artifact's real payload, re-fetched from `canonical_url`,\nrun through the existing deterministic gate, re-stamping `security_status` so enforce mode reflects\npayload truth. MONOTONIC toward non-servable. No LLM cost (deterministic detectors only; judge/sandbox\ndefault-off). NOTE (verified): payloads are NOT retained on disk (`payload_files` lazy + empty), so the\nscan must re-fetch â€” but the re-fetch+scan machinery already exists in\n`bin/run_security_shadow.py::_run_pipeline` (real `payload_extractor.extract` â†’ `fetcher.fetch_payload`,\n7-day tarball cache). H1 drives that same scan to ENFORCE-write `security_status`. Scannable set\n(`retired_at IS NULL AND kind IN ('skill','tool','agent','model')`) â‰ˆ 775 artifacts.\n\n**Deliverables:** `bin/scan_payload_depth.py` CLI running the real extractâ†’detectorsâ†’`scorer.score`\npipeline and persisting via `gate.write_verdict` in enforce mode (`run_judge=False,run_sandbox=False`);\na monotonic re-stamp guard (reuse `gate._worst_status`, write only when not a relaxation â€” clean\npayload = `clean-with-notes` = current value, so clean rows untouched; malicious â†’ quarantine/reject);\n`extraction_complete=False` â†’ fail-closed to `quarantine` only when not a relaxation, recorded as\n`extraction-incomplete`; `--limit N`, `--dry-run`, `--audit-out` (lists every verdict changed vs the\nW2 `served-text-v1` backfill); a regression test (benign-name/malicious-payload fixture: `clean-with-notes`\nafter W2, non-servable after payload-depth; a quarantined fixture never relaxed); an adversarial\nno-unearned-pass test (write path can never raise servability) + a CI assertion no new\n`security_status IN (...)` literal is introduced (single-owner test still passes).\n\n**Depends on:** â€”\n\n**done-when:** Every scannable artifact has a payload-depth `security_status` (or audited\n`extraction-incomplete` quarantine); the benign/malicious fixture is caught; the re-stamp is provably\nmonotonic; an audit lists every changed verdict; the single-owner gate test passes; `pytest` green, no\ntest weakening.\n\n- **Given** a benign-description/malicious-payload artifact, **when** the CLI runs in enforce mode, **then** its `security_status` becomes non-servable and it drops out of enforce-mode MCP/publisher queries.\n- **Given** an artifact already stricter-than-clean, **when** the scan computes a milder verdict, **then** the stricter prior holds (worst-wins) â€” no flagged artifact is silently re-admitted.\n- **Given** an unfetchable/stale URL, **then** the result is `extraction-incomplete`, fail-closed where not a relaxation, surfaced in the audit (never left servable on a failed fetch).\n\n## Wave 2 â€” H2: Evidence-loop promotion machinery (real score_fn, engine-diff CLI, tightened gate)\n\n**Intent:** Make the W3 evidence loop promotable: a real per-iteration LLM re-scoring `score_fn` over\nthe payload-deepened corpus (replacing `make_precomputed_score_fn`), a runnable `bin/engine-diff.py`\naround `roles/shadow_diff.py`, and a metered batch to populate `validations_shadow` (0