yload-depth`; ~506/775 no-payload artifacts (mostly arxiv) get `served-text-fallback`, not newly quarantined.\n- **W2/H2 â€” evidence-loop promotion machinery:** real metered per-iteration `make_live_score_fn`, `bin/engine-diff.py` GO/NO-GO gate (agreementâ‰¥0.95, samplesâ‰¥200, unearned==0, costâ‰¤1.5Ã—), budget-capped shadow batch. A BLOCKER (both reviewers agreed) caught the nightly shadow being silently swapped to the paid score_fn; FIX restored zero-cost nightly default, made `$0-shadow â†’ NO-GO`, adoption monotonic-toward-stricter.\n- **W3/L1 â€” cost-telemetry substrate:** migration `0024_costs_cache_batch.sql` + cache sub-rates (read â‰ˆ0.1Ã—, write â‰ˆ1.25Ã—) + `batch_discount: 0.5`; legacy 4-arg `CostRecorder.record` path provably byte-for-byte unchanged (verified against a 22,013-row live-DB copy).\n- **W5/L3 â€” structured outputs:** schema-guaranteed JSON via forced `emit_result` tool-use on critic/reconciler/judge; off-schema judge still fails closed to `abstain`; degrades to plain-text parse on any structured-call failure.\n- **W6/L4 â€” adaptive thinking via `effort`:** recursive `_assert_no_budget_tokens` guard before every Anthropic dispatch (Opus 4.8 400s on `budget_tokens`); `_fold_thinking_into_output` guards the prior $118 over-spend class. Default (effort unset) cost-neutral.\n\n## Honest tripwires â€” built but inert at current scale\n- **W4/L2 â€” prompt caching is a no-op for Aurora today:** all stable prefixes (15â€“317 tok) are 15â€“60Ã— below Anthropic's per-model cache minimums (Sonnet 2048 / Haiku 4096). Plumbing is correct and gated behind `cache_prefix_clears_minimum`; **no cost savings banked**.\n- **W7/L5 â€” model retargeting + tokenizer factor:** estimate helpers are **dead code** (Aurora budgets in fixed-USD, no token pre-flight consumer); defaults were already on current tiers. Narrow real value: `claude-opus-4-8` is now priced so an Opus override meters correctly instead of $0.\n- **W8/L6 â€” Message Batches API:** ready plumbing, **net-negative EV at current scale** â€” only critic_a wired (1 of 3 per-candidate calls), and the up-to-~65-min blocking poll outweighs sub-cent savings at TOP_K=2. Default-off; revisit only if TOP_K rises.\n- Collectively L2/L5/L6 are \"correct, honest, forward-ready plumbing that is largely INERT at Aurora's current prompt sizes + TOP_K=2\" â€” exactly the AuroraTwo research's \"validate before banking\" caveat, now measured.\n\n## Explicitly NOT run (separately-authorized, all gated default-off)\n- **H2 SA-1:** the metered shadow batch to populate `validations_shadow` (0 rows today, needs â‰¥200).\n- **H2 SA-2:** the live `AURORA_EVIDENCE_ENGINE=loop` flip (default stays `legacy`).\n- **H1 live re-stamp** against `kb/aurora.db` â€” the build delivers the CLI + tests only.\n\nWant me to save this as an Aurora project memory, or is it just for the handoff doc?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16013,"cache_read_input_tokens":32963,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16013},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3ebcf08-c961-4db6-8228-86ade240a49d","uuid":"24135c78-81d9-451c-ba4d-3caa78a79080","request_id":"req_011Cc1HkdVVTqWpiAVFHnGDN"}
